{"author":{"id":"40e3ba2788b3b9fc163c354afc44e5f9d225bcf0a27e679aaa878dd6135c6dcb"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777790115,"nonce":"Llr5BmGo6+J4fS4Xs6tU+5k6riI=","title":"Outreach: cultural mirror to git.sdf.org + SDF member page","message":"Mirror UC2 to git.sdf.org and link from SDF member page (~evv) as the user's flagship preservation project. The SDF retrocomputing/old-Unix culture is the most aligned community for a UC2 revival; tribal-membership signal that GitHub cannot provide.\n\nSteps:\n1. Upgrade SDF account from ARPA to MetaARPA ($44/yr) — required for git.sdf.org access. UC2 alone may not justify this; bundle with GW-BASIC 2026, freeclaw, and other preservation projects to amortize the cost across multiple uses (also unlocks: personal cron, screen, IRC proxy, SSL on ~evv site, NNTP posting).\n2. Create git.sdf.org/evv/uc2 mirror; add as 'sdf' remote in local repo; configure cron or post-receive hook on primary remote to push.\n3. Build SDF member page at member.sdf.org/~evv (or chosen alias) listing preservation projects with brief descriptions and links. UC2 as the flagship.\n4. Add 'Mirrors' section to UC2 README listing GitHub (primary), git.sdf.org (cultural mirror), and Software Heritage (institutional archive).\n5. Bonus: post brief project announcement to SDF bboard (bboard from shell prompt) — small audience, perfectly aligned.\n\nCodeberg as alternative or additional mirror: better OSS discovery than SDF, no membership required, similar 'we don't trust GitHub long-term' signal. Consider both rather than one or the other.\n\nThis issue is bundled-low-priority on its own; promotes to medium if MetaARPA is acquired for other reasons.","files":null}]}